    <h1>About Prayer Hub</h1>
    <div class="prayer-section">
      <p>Prayer Hub is an independent, free library of Christian prayers, in the Catholic tradition, for every part of the day: morning and night, healing and protection, the saints, novenas and the Psalms.</p>

      <h2>Where our texts come from</h2>
      <p><strong>Traditional prayers</strong> (such as the Prayer to Saint Michael, the Morning Offering or the Memorare) are given in their customary English wording, with their origin noted on the page.</p>
      <p><strong>Scripture</strong> is quoted from the King James Version, which is in the public domain, with the reference for every verse.</p>
      <p><strong>New prayers and reflections</strong> are written by the Prayer Hub team to accompany the traditional texts. They are not official liturgical texts of any Church.</p>

      <h2>Corrections</h2>
      <p>If you spot an error in a prayer, a Scripture reference or a date, please tell us through our page on X and we will correct it. Every page shows the date it was last updated.</p>
    </div>
  </article>
